cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Strict local maximality of Gerver's moving sofa: a computer-assisted Sobolev coercivity argument"
authors:
  - family-names: Bonfioli
    given-names: Vico
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-05-29
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ElVec1o/moving-sofa-local-max"
abstract: >
  A computer-assisted argument that Joseph Gerver's 1992 candidate sofa
  is a strict local maximum of the area functional on the Sobolev space
  H^2 of corner trajectories, modulo translation symmetry. The
  coercivity constant satisfies m >= 4.34 in the H^2-norm; the
  trajectory is the unique critical point in an explicit H^2-ball of
  radius >= 0.0456. Three ingredients are not yet rigorous and are
  flagged throughout: (i) the finite-dimensional Hessian is evaluated
  with a floating-point polygon-intersection oracle (Shapely) rather
  than true interval arithmetic; (ii) the cross-term coupling between
  low and high Fourier modes is bounded by a numerical placeholder
  rather than an analytic estimate; (iii) the second variation Q
  decomposes as Q_smooth + Q_jump, where Lemma 8 characterizes Q_smooth
  analytically but Q_jump (from the four contact-transition breakpoints)
  is captured only empirically by the polygon Hessian computation.
keywords:
  - moving sofa problem
  - Gerver's sofa
  - local maximality
  - second variation
  - computer-assisted
